# 🌸 English Contemplation

Sumit Patel Ji beautifully points toward the final transition in spiritual life.

At first, we purify the mind.

Then we discipline the senses.

Then we practice selfless action.

All of this is essential.

Yet Advaita asks one final question:

**Who is the one claiming to purify?**

Karma Yoga refines the instrument.

Vedānta reveals the Player was never the instrument.

Action continues.

Duty continues.

Compassion continues.

But the imaginary owner quietly disappears.

The body acts.

The mind thinks.

Life unfolds.

Yet no separate doer can be found.

That is not inactivity.

It is **freedom in the midst of activity.**

The highest realization is not becoming inactive.

It is recognizing that the Self has **never** been an actor.

It has always been the silent, luminous Presence in which all actions appear and disappear.

